From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 22:46:30 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] panda: main_loop_wait callback at each main-loop iteration

pandare2 runs its queued main-loop work (snap, revert_async, cont) from
this callback; it had no call site.  It runs after main_loop_should_exit()
and not while a stop request waits (a vCPU callback asks for the stop,
then queues the work), and outside main_loop_wait itself, so savevm and
loadvm are not nested in an aio dispatch.

SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
Origin: new
---
 system/runstate.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/system/runstate.c b/system/runstate.c
index 2f596b449363b6d53505bf958c6620ca498813de..61adbf7d98d557b37ee258ba49f80d5d521af3f8 100644
--- a/system/runstate.c
+++ b/system/runstate.c
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@
 #include "system/replay.h"
 #include "system/reset.h"
 #include "system/runstate.h"
+#include "panda/hooks.h"
 #include "system/runstate-action.h"
 #include "system/confidential-guest-support.h"
 #include "system/system.h"
@@ -950,6 +951,13 @@ int qemu_main_loop(void)
     int status = EXIT_SUCCESS;
 
     while (!main_loop_should_exit(&status)) {
+        /*
+         * Not while a stop request waits: a vCPU callback asks for the stop
+         * before it queues work for here (savevm, loadvm, cont).
+         */
+        if (vmstop_requested == RUN_STATE__MAX) {
+            panda_callbacks_main_loop_wait();
+        }
         main_loop_wait(false);
     }
 
